# Agent Behavior Guidelines

## Read first
- Read `CLAUDE.md` (repository root) before working. It lists the absolute rules (never commit/merge/push to `main`/`develop`, never commit secrets or personal data — this repository is public), the project structure, and the documents to read next (`docs/prompts/_common-context.md`, `docs/prompts/_commands.md`).

## Language
- **Japanese (日本語)**: This is the primary language for this project.
- All explanations, documents, code comments and docstrings must be written in Japanese. Identifiers stay in English.

## Execution Environment
- **Docker**: Always run commands (including tests, linting, and scripts) inside the Docker container.
- Use `docker compose exec shinouta-time <command>` or `docker compose run --rm shinouta-time <command>`.
- Do not run commands directly on the host machine unless explicitly instructed. Exceptions: `git` and `sh tools/check-rules.sh` (the container has no git).
